==History==
2017
*The Heal was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Heal Draft Challenge]], which started on 28/4/2017. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Heal. If the player achieved at least 6 wins, they obtained the Heal early {{Balance|Add}}.
*The Heal [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 1/5/2017 {{Balance|Add}}.
*On 12/6/2017, the [[Version History#June 2017 Update (12/6/2017)|June 2017 Update]], allowed multiple Heal [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] to stack {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 11/8/2017, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (11/8/2017)|Balance Update]], decreased its duration to 2.5 seconds (from 3.05 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}. This also fixed inconsistencies where the Heal healed either six pulses or seven pulses; it will now pulse exactly five times, in effect decreasing its effectiveness by two-sevenths {{Balance|Neutral}}.
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], allowed the Heal to be placed on the river {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], increased the Heal's area radius to 4 tiles (from 3 tiles) {{Balance|Buff}}. It also moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Heal from Hog Mountain to Royal Arena {{Balance|Buff}}.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Rare}} cards start at Level 3 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 11) {{Balance|Neutral}}.
2019
*On 7/1/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/1/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Heal’s cost to 1 [[Elixir]] (from 3 Elixir) {{Balance|Buff}}, decreased its duration to 2 seconds (from 2.5 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}, and decreased its healing by 63% {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], removed the Heal from all [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Draft]] selections {{Balance|Remove}}.
*On 4/11/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (4/11/2019)|Balance Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Heal from Royal Arena to Hog Mountain {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], removed the Heal from [[Touchdown]] Draft {{Balance|Remove}}.
2020
*On 2/4/2020, a [[Version History#Maintenance%20Break%20(2/4/2020)|maintenance break]], replaced the Heal with the [[Heal Spirit]] {{Balance|Remove}}.

==Trivia==
*The Heal is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Lightning]], [[Freeze]], [[Poison]], [[Rage]], and [[Clone]].
**In Clash Royale, it is simply just called "Heal" but in Clash of Clans, it is called "Healing".
*The Heal, along with [[Skeletons]], [[Electro Spirit]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Warmth]], and [[Heal Spirit]], are the cheapest [[cards]], costing 1 [[Elixir]]. Also, along with the Warmth, the Heal is the cheapest spell card, and along with Heal Spirit, the cheapest {{Rarity|Rare}} card.
*In the French, German, Spanish, Norwegian, Russian, Arabic, Portuguese, Persian and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Heal's name translates to "Healing". In the Italian, Turkish, Korean, Chinese, and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Heal's name translates to "Treatment", "Restoration", "Healing Magic", "Healing Spell", and "Healer" respectively.
*The Heal has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Heal is 1 of 4 spells that have been featured in the [[Global Spell]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Lightning, Freeze, and Rage.
**The Heal is 1 of 3 spells that has been featured in the Boost Fields game mode, the others being Rage and Clone.
**The Heal is 1 of 5 spells that have been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Spell%20Cauldron|Spell Cauldron]] sub-mode of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Lightning, Freeze, Rage, and Clone.
*The Heal is 1 of 23 cards that has had its Elixir cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], Fire Spirit, [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], Rage, [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*The icon of the "Healer" [[Card Mastery]] task resembles a Heal spell.
*The Heal, along with the Lightning, Freeze, Rage, and [[The Log]], are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Spells spell] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*It is the first card to be [[:Category:Removed Cards|removed]] from the game.
**The replacement card, the Heal Spirit, references that in a line of text below the description which reads "''R.I.P. Heal. 2017 - 2020. Alas, we hardly used ye.''", referring to the Heal's extremely low usage rate in both casual and competitive play.

